oic_consistency":0.8327861012647612,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.2390994499567688,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":96.4,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.0726263036158305,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":57.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06659353853610561,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":58.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.4883292801535466,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.006085871351554073,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":56.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.054445078283027436,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":71.6,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.021631068033975742,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":77.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.005700325732899023,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":90.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.00096000003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ConocoPhillips explores for, produces, transports, and markets crude oil, bitumen, natural gas, liquefied natural gas (LNG), and natural gas liquids. It operates in five segments: Alaska; Lower 48; Canada; Europe, Middle East and North Africa; and Asia Pacific. The company's portfolio includes unconventional plays in North America; conventional assets in North America, Europe, Asia, and Australia; global LNG developments; oil sands assets in Canada; and an inventory of global exploration prospects. It serves in the United States, Canada, China, Equatorial Guinea, Libya, Malaysia, Norway, Singapore, the United Kingdom, and internationally. ConocoPhillips was founded in 1917 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew M. O'Brien | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $6.1M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers, declining at 6%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Stock-based compensation of $35K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["ConocoPhillips is a large-cap energy business with a $163.7B market cap on $58.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","Accruals are elevated at -9.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 82% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8220337461458688},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $20.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["44 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ConocoPhillips (NYSE:COP) Announces Earnings Results, Beats Expectations By $0.22 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/conocophillips-nysecop-announces-earnings-results-beats-expectations-by-0-22-eps.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988648.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"COP Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Cash Flow Growth and Lower Spending","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/cop-q3-earnings-call-highlights-140400240.html","date":"2026-11-06